{"id":"mahabharata-3-100","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":100,"title":"शततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 100 · The Kalakeyas ravage the world","summary":{"en":"From their refuge in the sea the Kalakeyas come out by night and kill the sages in their hermitages, so that sacrifices cease and the world is terrified. The gods go to Vishnu for protection.","kn":"ಸಮುದ್ರದ ಆಶ್ರಯದಿಂದ ಕಾಲಕೇಯರು ರಾತ್ರಿ ಹೊರಬಂದು ಆಶ್ರಮಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಋಷಿಗಳನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಯಜ್ಞಗಳು ನಿಲ್ಲುತ್ತವೆ, ಲೋಕ ಭಯಗೊಳ್ಳುತ್ತದೆ. ದೇವತೆಗಳು ರಕ್ಷಣೆಗಾಗಿ ವಿಷ್ಣುವಿನಲ್ಲಿಗೆ ಹೋಗುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"समुद्र में अपने आश्रय से कालकेय रात में निकलकर आश्रमों में ऋषियों को मार डालते हैं, जिससे यज्ञ रुक जाते हैं और संसार भयभीत होता है। देवता रक्षा के लिए विष्णु के पास जाते हैं।","te":"సముద్ర ఆశ్రయం నుండి కాలకేయులు రాత్రి బయటకు వచ్చి ఆశ్రమాలలో ఋషులను చంపుతారు, యజ్ఞాలు ఆగిపోతాయి, లోకం భయపడుతుంది. దేవతలు రక్షణ కోసం విష్ణువు వద్దకు వెళ్తారు.","ta":"கடலில் ஒளிந்த காலகேயர்கள் இரவில் வெளிவந்து ஆசிரமங்களில் முனிவர்களைக் கொல்ல, யாகங்கள் நின்று உலகம் அஞ்சுகிறது. தேவர்கள் காவலுக்காக விஷ்ணுவிடம் செல்கிறார்கள்.","ml":"കടലിലെ ഒളിത്താവളത്തിൽനിന്ന് രാത്രിയിൽ പുറത്തുവരുന്ന കാലകേയന്മാർ ആശ്രമങ്ങളിൽ ഋഷിമാരെ കൊല്ലുന്നു; യാഗങ്ങൾ നിലയ്ക്കുകയും ലോകം ഭയചകിതമാകുകയും ചെയ്യുന്നു. സംരക്ഷണത്തിനായി ദേവന്മാർ വിഷ്ണുവിന്റെ അടുത്തേക്ക് പോകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.100; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"तीर्थयात्रापर्व","titleEn":"Tirthayatra Parva (The pilgrimage)","verses":[{"text":"लोमश उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Lomasha said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"समुद्रं ते समाश्रित्य वारुणं निधिमम्भसाम् ।\nकालेयाः संप्रवर्तन्त त्रैलोक्यस्य विनाशने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking refuge in the sea, Varuna's treasury of waters, the Kaleyas set out to destroy the three worlds."}},{"n":2,"text":"ते रात्रौ समभिक्रुद्धा भक्षयन्ति सदा मुनीन् ।\nआश्रमेषु च ये सन्ति पुन्येष्वायतनेषु च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Enraged, at night they always devoured the sages who were in hermitages and holy places."}},{"n":3,"text":"वसिष्ठस्याश्रमे विप्रा भक्षितास्तैर्दुरात्मभिः ।\nअशीतिशतमष्टौ च नव चान्ये तपस्विनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those wicked ones devoured brahmins in Vasishtha's hermitage: eight hundred and ninety other ascetics."}},{"n":4,"text":"च्यवनस्याश्रमं गत्वा पुण्यं द्विजनिषेवितम् ।\nफलमूलाशनानां हि मुनीनां भक्षितं शतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going to Chyavana's holy hermitage, visited by brahmins, they ate a hundred sages who lived on fruit and roots."}},{"n":5,"text":"एवं रात्रौ स्म कुर्वन्ति विविशुश्चार्णवं दिवा ।\nभरद्वाजाश्रमे चैव नियता ब्रह्मचारिणः ।\nवाय्वाहाराम्बुभक्षाश्च विंशतिः संनिपातिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So they did by night and entered the sea by day. In Bharadvaja's hermitage they slew twenty disciplined students, who lived on air and water."}},{"n":6,"text":"एवं क्रमेण सर्वांस्तानाश्रमान्दानवास्तदा ।\nनिशायां परिधावन्ति मत्ता भुजबलाश्रयात् ।\nकालोपसृष्टाः कालेया घ्नन्तो द्विजगणान्बहून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this way, in order, the drunken Danavas ran through all the hermitages at night, relying on the strength of their arms, killing many brahmins, the Kaleyas driven by fate."}},{"n":7,"text":"न चैनानन्वबुध्यन्त मनुजा मनुजोत्तम ।\nएवं प्रवृत्तान्दैत्यांस्तांस्तापसेषु तपस्विषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of men, men did not understand it. The Daityas thus pursued the ascetics in their austerities."}},{"n":8,"text":"प्रभाते समदृश्यन्त नियताहारकर्शिताः ।\nमहीतलस्था मुनयः शरीरैर्गतजीवितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the morning the sages were seen lying on the ground, wasted by their restricted food, with bodies bereft of life."}},{"n":9,"text":"क्षीणमांसैर्विरुधिरैर्विमज्जान्त्रैर्विसंधिभिः ।\nआकीर्णैराचिता भूमिः शङ्खानामिव राशिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With flesh wasted, bloodless, marrowless, with entrails gone and joints loosened, the earth was covered with scattered bodies, like heaps of conch shells."}},{"n":10,"text":"कलशैर्विप्रविद्धैश्च स्रुवैर्भग्नैस्तथैव च ।\nविकीर्णैरग्निहोत्रैश्च भूर्बभूव समावृता ॥","meaning":{"en":"The ground was strewn with broken pitchers, shattered ladles and scattered sacred fires."}},{"n":11,"text":"निःस्वाध्यायवषट्कारं नष्टयज्ञोत्सवक्रियम् ।\nजगदासीन्निरुत्साहं कालेयभयपीडितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The world, without Vedic study or the sacrificial cry, with its sacrifices and festivals ruined, lost its spirit, tormented by fear of the Kaleyas."}},{"n":12,"text":"एवं प्रक्षीयमाणाश्च मानवा मनुजेश्वर ।\nआत्मत्राणपरा भीताः प्राद्रवन्त दिशो भयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus, as people were destroyed, lord of men, they fled in fear in all directions, intent on saving themselves."}},{"n":13,"text":"केचिद्गुहाः प्रविविशुर्निर्झरांश्चापरे श्रिताः ।\nअपरे मरणोद्विग्ना भयात्प्रानान्समुत्सृजन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some entered caves, some took shelter by waterfalls, and others, troubled by fear of death, gave up life."}},{"n":14,"text":"केचिदत्र महेष्वासाः शूराः परमदर्पिताः ।\nमार्गमाणाः परं यत्नं दानवानां प्रचक्रिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some brave great archers, very proud, made great efforts searching for the Danavas."}},{"n":15,"text":"न चैतानधिजग्मुस्ते समुद्रं समुपाश्रितान् ।\nश्रमं जग्मुश्च परममाजग्मुः क्षयमेव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"But they could not find them, as they had taken refuge in the sea, and the heroes grew very weary and some perished."}},{"n":16,"text":"जगत्युपशमं याते नष्टयज्ञोत्सवक्रिये ।\nआजग्मुः परमामार्तिं त्रिदशा मनुजेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the world fell silent, its sacrifices and festivals lost, the gods, lord of men, fell into great distress."}},{"n":17,"text":"समेत्य समहेन्द्राश्च भयान्मन्त्रं प्रचक्रिरे ।\nनारायणं पुरस्कृत्य वैकुण्ठमपराजितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gathering with Indra, in fear they took counsel, putting at their head Narayana of Vaikuntha, the unconquered."}},{"n":18,"text":"ततो देवाः समेतास्ते तदोचुर्मधुसूदनम् ।\nत्वं नः स्रष्टा च पाता च भर्ता च जगतः प्रभो ।\nत्वया सृष्टमिदं सर्वं यच्चेङ्गं यच्च नेङ्गति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the assembled gods said to Madhusudana: \"Lord, you are creator, protector and sustainer of the world. All this, moving and unmoving, was made by you."}},{"n":19,"text":"त्वया भूमिः पुरा नष्टा समुद्रात्पुष्करेक्षण ।\nवाराहं रूपमास्थाय जगदर्थे समुद्धृता ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Lotus-eyed one, long ago you lifted the lost earth from the sea in the form of a boar, for the world's sake."}},{"n":20,"text":"आदिदैत्यो महावीर्यो हिरण्यकशिपुस्त्वया ।\nनारसिंहं वपुः कृत्वा सूदितः पुरुषोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Best of persons, you took the form of a man-lion and killed Hiranyakashipu, the great and mighty first Daitya."}},{"n":21,"text":"अवध्यः सर्वभूतानां बलिश्चापि महासुरः ।\nवामनं वपुराश्रित्य त्रैलोक्याद्भ्रंशितस्त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The great asura Bali, whom no creature could kill, you cast down from his hold on the three worlds by taking the dwarf form."}},{"n":22,"text":"असुरश्च महेष्वासो जम्भ इत्यभिविश्रुतः ।\nयज्ञक्षोभकरः क्रूरस्त्वयैव विनिपातितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The cruel great archer asura called Jambha, who disrupted sacrifices, was struck down by you alone."}},{"n":23,"text":"एवमादीनि कर्माणि येषां संख्या न विद्यते ।\nअस्माकं भयभीतानां त्वं गतिर्मधुसूदन ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"There are countless deeds of yours like these. Madhusudana, you are the refuge of us, frightened as we are."}},{"n":24,"text":"तस्मात्त्वां देव देवेश लोकार्थं ज्ञापयामहे ।\nरक्ष लोकांश्च देवांश्च शक्रं च महतो भयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Therefore, god, lord of gods, we make this known to you for the world's sake: protect the worlds, the gods and Indra from this great fear.\""}}]}]}